    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22388" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inclīnābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		inclino, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that readily leans to</i> any thing, <i>prone.</i>—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in pravum inclinabiles animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 94, 40</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Not to be moved</i> or <i>bent</i>
			(lat. Lat.): atque immobilis permansit, (Hilar.) Anon. in Job, 1, p.
			104.</div>
